@baseUrl = https://localhost:7179
@adminEmail = utkucakar@hotmail.com
# Type your AdminUser:Password (user secrets) here while testing. Do not commit it
@adminPassword = CHANGE_ME
# A throwaway customer for development, not a secret. Register it once with CUSTOMER-1
@customerEmail = alice@test.com
@customerPassword = alice-password-123

### AUTH) Login as admin. Send this first: the admin requests below read the token from its response
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{adminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{adminPassword}}"
}


### CUSTOMER-1) Register the customer once (409 from the second time on)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}"
}

### CUSTOMER-2) Login as the customer. The customer requests below read the token from its response
# @name customer
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{customerEmail}}",
  "password": "{{customerPassword}}"
}

### 1) List all passengers (admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/passengers
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### 1b) My passengers: use these ids below. Passengers created before Adım 23c belong to nobody → 404 for a customer
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/passengers/mine
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 2) Add passenger to my account (Deney D1: send this twice)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/passengers
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Nura",
  "lastName": "Çakar",
  "email": "nuray@example.com",
  "passportNumber": "TR7654321"
}

### 3) Get passenger by id: the response's ETag header is its version
# @name passengerToEdit
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/passengers/1
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 4) Update passenger. Send 3 first: If-Match carries its ETag
# Without If-Match → 428. With an old ETag (someone saved in between) → 412
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/passengers/1
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: {{passengerToEdit.response.headers.ETag}}

{
  "firstName": "Ayşe",
  "lastName": "Yılmaz Kaya",
  "email": "ayse@example.com",
  "passportNumber": "TR1234567"
}

### 5) Delete passenger with a reservation (Restrict → 500 for now)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/passengers/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 6) Non-existent passenger
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/passengers/999
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 7) Adım 8: invalid passenger (expect 400 with errors)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/passengers
Authorization: Bearer {{customer.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "",
  "lastName": "Bu soyad elli karakterden çok daha uzun olduğu için reddedilmeli mutlaka",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "passportNumber": ""
}
